  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Wind Energy Conference</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Wind Energy Association (WWEA) and The Energy and Resources Institute (TERI), with the support of the International Solar Alliance (ISA) and International Solar Energy Society (ISES), are jointly hosting World Wind Energy Conference 2021 (WWEC2021) during 24-26 November 2021, in New Delhi, India, in a virtual format with a theme &#x2018;Powering the World with Wind and Sun&#x2019;. It will be a knowledge and industry platform to capture learnings from various parts of the world and in return leading to India&#x2019;s vision of Atmanirbhar Bharat aiming at self-reliance in technology and manufacturing, not only to meet domestic requirements but also for the country to emerge as a regional hub for the export of renewable energy systems and services.</narrative>
  </description>
